WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.238 --> 00:00:07.100
Up in the mountains, a man entered a cave.

2
00:00:07.101 --> 00:00:10.976
He walked through a long, dark tunnel.

3
00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:18.808
His flashlight lit up stone doors in the wall.

4
00:00:18.809 --> 00:00:26.626
He pushed a door open and stepped into a large room.

5
00:00:26.627 --> 00:00:30.682
The man gasped. "He's real!"

6
00:00:30.683 --> 00:00:34.074
A giant caveman lay on a large, flat stone.

7
00:00:34.075 --> 00:00:36.745
He was perfectly still.

8
00:00:36.746 --> 00:00:40.927
The man walked over and pulled a gold ring from his bag.

9
00:00:40.928 --> 00:00:42.797
He took a deep breath.

10
00:00:42.798 --> 00:00:52.446
"Now I'll find out if the legend is true."

11
00:00:52.447 --> 00:00:55.608
"I'm done," Mara said.

12
00:00:55.609 --> 00:01:00.612
"I wrote five facts about wooly mammoths."

13
00:01:00.613 --> 00:01:03.156
Roxy and her friends were on a field trip.

14
00:01:03.157 --> 00:01:07.067
Their class was visiting Metro City Natural History Museum.

15
00:01:07.068 --> 00:01:09.034
Everyone had to choose a topic.

16
00:01:09.035 --> 00:01:12.462
Then they had to write down five facts about it.

17
00:01:12.463 --> 00:01:14.285
Roxy was already done.

18
00:01:14.286 --> 00:01:17.820
Her topic was saber-toothed tigers.

19
00:01:17.821 --> 00:01:21.449
"Let's go to the astronomy wing now," Terrell said.

20
00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:24.944
"I'm going to write about meteorites.

21
00:01:24.945 --> 00:01:29.574
Jack still has to find something to write about."

22
00:01:29.575 --> 00:01:31.557
"Check it out," Jack said.

23
00:01:31.558 --> 00:01:35.038
"I can balance a pencil on the tip of my nose."

24
00:01:35.039 --> 00:01:41.155
He looked up and stood the pencil on his nose. "Whoa, whoa . . . ugh!"

25
00:01:41.156 --> 00:01:44.817
The pencil fell from his nose and rolled across the floor.

26
00:01:44.818 --> 00:01:51.114
Mara snorted. "You only balanced it for about a second."

27
00:01:51.115 --> 00:01:58.239
Jack tried again. "I'm doing it! I'm doing it!" The pencil fell again.

28
00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:02.997
Terrell shook his head. "That wasn't even a second."

29
00:02:02.998 --> 00:02:09.429
"Jack!" Miss Apricot hurried over. "Did you pick a topic yet?"

30
00:02:09.430 --> 00:02:13.975
Jack grinned sheepishly. "Not yet, Miss Apricot."

31
00:02:13.976 --> 00:02:16.380
Miss Apricot folded her arms.

32
00:02:16.381 --> 00:02:21.659
"Please stop goofing around. And find something to write about."

33
00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:23.836
Miss Apricot walked away.

34
00:02:23.837 --> 00:02:29.073
Jack sighed. "Maybe Rocket Girl can help me."

35
00:02:29.074 --> 00:02:34.850
Roxy laughed. "You don't need Rocket Girl's help with your topic."

36
00:02:34.851 --> 00:02:39.656
"No," Jack said. "I mean she could help me balance this pencil."

37
00:02:39.657 --> 00:02:43.870
Everyone laughed.

38
00:02:43.871 --> 00:02:47.824
"That's ridiculous, Jack," Mara said.

39
00:02:47.825 --> 00:02:53.374
Roxy's watch beeped.

40
00:02:53.375 --> 00:02:58.416
She stepped away from her friends.

41
00:02:58.417 --> 00:03:02.340
"Mayor Bloom," she whispered. "What's wrong?"

42
00:03:02.341 --> 00:03:04.666
"Rocket Girl," Mayor Bloom said.

43
00:03:04.667 --> 00:03:09.930
"A valuable artifact is missing from Metro City Natural History Museum.

44
00:03:09.931 --> 00:03:12.117
It was in the North American wing.

45
00:03:12.118 --> 00:03:16.148
I need you to go and find out what happened."

46
00:03:16.149 --> 00:03:20.756
Roxy looked around. "Okay, Mayor."

47
00:03:20.757 --> 00:03:22.914
Mayor Bloom looked confused.

48
00:03:22.915 --> 00:03:27.525
"Um, aren't you going to say that you're on your way?"

49
00:03:27.526 --> 00:03:31.641
Roxy chuckled. "I'm already here, Mayor.

50
00:03:31.642 --> 00:03:34.399
Our class has a field trip today.

51
00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:40.417
But don't worry—I'll find that artifact."

